body:
I suggest fix along these lines (PHP seems to cast to integers  indices like '1' or '23', but not ' 1' or '01'), so comparing type to `integer` seems to be a reliable method:

```
  if ((1 === $keysCount && '0' == $keys[0])
            || ($keysCount > 1 && array_reduce($keys, function ($carry, $item) {
                    if ( $carry === null ) return; // null carry is error
                    if ( 'integer' !== gettype($item) ) {
                        return null;
                    }
                    return (int) $carry + $item;
                }, 0) === $keysCount * ($keysCount - 1) / 2)
        )
```
